  "reason": "The assistant directly contradicts the legal provisions stated in the REFERENCE by asserting that all employees automatically receive five weeks of vacation regardless of age, and that adults over 20 are entitled to the same amount as younger workers, which conflicts with OR Art. 329a (minimum four weeks, five weeks only for those up to completed 20th year) and OR Art. 329d(2).",
  "evidence": "Ja, in der Schweiz erhalten Arbeitnehmer in der Regel mindestens fünf Wochen Ferien pro Jahr, unabhängig von ihrem Alter. Erwachsene über 20 Jahre sind somit ebenso berechtigt, diese Ferien zu nehmen, wie jüngere Arbeitnehmer."
